# Development happens on Windows; everything here runs on Linux (tars-prod).
# Two things break when that isn't enforced:
#   1. CRLF endings — a CRLF shebang fails with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M".
#   2. The exec bit — Windows checkouts don't carry it, so `git reset --hard`
#      in deploy.sh can strip +x from a script systemd invokes via ExecStart.
#      That silently killed tars-backup.service from 2026-05-31 to 2026-08-10
#      (status=203/EXEC), so the exec bits are now pinned in the index.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.timer     text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
